cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on the Nano-Commons Protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "The Nano-Commons Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A protocol for tiny autonomous agents that run on volunteer and edge
  computers. Results are signed, cross-checked by independent nodes, weighted
  by earned reputation, capped so that no region decides alone, and audited
  against canary tasks with known answers. Owned by everyone; no token; no
  central server.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Krittidet
    family-names: Chanthake
    role: "Initiator and Genesis Author"
  - name: "The Nano-Commons contributors"
version: "0.2.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - decentralised AI
  - public good
  - verifiable computation
  - canary tasks
  - commons
